<title>POLAND: Kable soars on investor plans to up stake.</title>
<headline>Kable soars on investor plans to up stake.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish cable maker Kable SA surged 9.7-percent in a moderate 1.7-million-zloty turnover on news that Denmark's NKT Cables plans to increase its stake in the firm to over 50 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The surge can be connected with the news that NKT Cables wants to increase stake in Kable and given that the stock was falling recently I'm not surprised it jumped,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Analysts said the stock was likely to extend its gains in the next few sessions.</p>
<p>On Friday the Polish Securities Commission approved the sale of a 25-percent stake of Kable to NKT Cables which would give NKT more than 50 percent of the Polish firm.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
